 "units": "mm, Z up",
 "origin_convention": "Each single-part STL in wip/v3od/stl/ is in its own native CAD coordinates. Apply each instance's transform to that STL as-is: world = location @ rotation @ native. Euler is Blender 'XYZ' order (same as Blender object rotation_euler); matrix_4x4 is the exact transform, use it if in doubt. Clamp: origin at post axis, bottom face at z=0, clamp ledge toward +Y. Frame: tall post axis at x=0, short post axis at x=533.4, both bottoms at z=0, frame in the XZ plane. Shelf/planter/extras: centred in XY, underside at z=0. Panels: centred in X, back face y=0, bottom z=0. Connector: centred on the joint, plug runs along Z.",
